            <ArticleTitle>Drug-induced augmentation of coronary flow in vessels with maximum ischemic dilatation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>66-76</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The possibility of drug-induced augmentation of coronary flow in vessels with maximum ischemic dilation has been investigated in anesthetized dogs. The auotperfused left anterior descending coronary artery was gradually narrowed to a &quot;critical&quot; degree at which hyperemic response to coronary occulsion was completely abolished...</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
